  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a VoiceOver user, I want a row's info line to say « Sondage » and « page 3 sur 12 » rather than read (or skip) the glyphs « ≣ » and « ⚑ », so that I know a topic is a poll and where my flag is.\n\n### Rule\n\n\"Provide alternative labels for all key interface elements. […] Add labels to any custom elements your app defines.\" — [HIG › VoiceOver](https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/voiceover) (Descriptions).\n\n### What the app does (dev-swift @ `7a61018f`)\n\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Navigation/TopicRowCues.swift:34`: `\"⚑\\(topic.isPoll ? \" \\u{2263}\" : \"\") \\(current) / \\(topic.pageCount)\"`; `Navigation/TopicRowInfoLine.swift:11-12` appends `\" \\u{2263}\"` after « N pages ». Both are plain `Text` inside a combined element (`Navigation/LegacyTopicRowView.swift:44-52`), with no `accessibilityLabel`.\n- In the default row « ≣ » is the only sign that a topic is a poll; the experimental dense row has a labelled « Sondage » icon (`Experimental/DenseRows/DenseTopicRowView.swift:45`).\n- Same « ⚑ page / max » on a group MP row (`Messages/MessageRowInfoLine.swift`).\n\n### Legacy at `87fe0d1c`\n\nSame strings, no label: `HFRswift/Swift/MainWindow.swift:469`, `:472`.\n\n### Class\n\n**(a) defect** if the Mac check confirms it (accessibility, shared with legacy); otherwise close.\n\n### Proposed fix and check\n\n- An `accessibilityLabel` on the info `Text` (e.g. « Sondage, page 3 sur 12 »).\n- Mac check first: what VoiceOver (French) says on a flagged poll row. If it already reads something meaningful, close this issue.\n\nFound by #866 (cloud/r866-fable, Fable 5.2)",
